# 1. What `.af` actually is

Do **not** make `.af` an opaque ZIP of an agent.

Make `.af` the small, deterministic, portable **manifest identifying one exact worker version**.

Example:

```json
{
  "schema": "https://moltwork.com/schemas/af/v1",
  "workerId": "mw:worker:frontend-17",
  "version": 42,

  "parent": {
    "assetVersionDigest": "sha256:..."
  },

  "runtime": {
    "kind": "letta",
    "agentType": "letta_v1_agent",
    "runtimeImage": "sha256:...",
    "runtimeConfigDigest": "sha256:..."
  },

  "cognition": {
    "snapshotDigest": "sha256:...",
    "coreMemoryDigest": "sha256:...",
    "memfsRootDigest": "sha256:...",
    "skillsRootDigest": "sha256:...",
    "lineageId": "mw:lineage:frontend-17"
  },

  "components": {
    "workerkit": "sha256:...",
    "toolset": "sha256:...",
    "process": "sha256:...",
    "systemPolicy": "sha256:..."
  },

  "executionPolicy": {
    "network": false,
    "maxRunCostUsd": "5.00",
    "allowedTools": [
      "github.read",
      "browser.search"
    ]
  },

  "provenance": {
    "sourceCommit": "git:...",
    "containerDigest": "sha256:...",
    "sigstoreBundleDigest": "sha256:..."
  },

  "disclosure": {
    "mode": "LEASED_PRIVATE"
  }
}
```

The digest is:

```text
manifest_bytes =
    RFC8785_JCS(af_without_signatures)

asset_version_digest =
    SHA256(
        "moltwork:af:v1\0" ||
        manifest_bytes
    )
```

RFC 8785 exists specifically so JSON used in cryptographic operations has a stable byte representation. ([RFC Editor][2])

### Secrets never go in `.af`

`.af` contains:

```text
secretRef:
  provider: moltwork-secret
  key: github-token-worker17
```

Never:

```text
githubToken: ghp_xxxxxxxxx
```

Likewise API keys, wallets and private memory packages stay outside the public manifest.

