# 6. DSSE is the signature layer

This is better than inventing:

```text
signature = sign(json.dumps(receipt))
```

DSSE authenticates both the payload bytes and their payload type and deliberately avoids making its signature mechanism dependent on parsing/canonicalizing the payload. ([GitHub][5])

Result:

```text
receipt.statement.json
        │
        ▼
      DSSE
        │
        ▼
receipt.dsse.json
```

Conceptually:

```json
{
  "payloadType":
    "application/vnd.in-toto+json",

  "payload":
    "BASE64(...)",

  "signatures": [
    {
      "keyid": "mw:worker:17:receipt",
      "sig": "..."
    }
  ]
}
```

Use:

```text
DSSE for runtime/run signatures
Sigstore/Cosign for software/build signatures
```

Do not merge those jobs.

