# 7. Sigstore protects what code was deployed

The build pipeline should be:

```text
Git commit
   │
   ▼
GitHub Actions
   │
   ▼
container
   │
   ▼
sha256:imageDigest
   │
   ▼
Cosign signature
   │
   ▼
Sigstore bundle / Rekor
   │
   ▼
digest-pinned dstack deployment
```

Sigstore keyless signing associates a short-lived signing key with an OIDC identity; the signing event can then be placed in Rekor's append-only transparency log. ([GitHub][6])

That proves:

> this container came from this build identity/source pipeline.

It does **not** prove:

> this container successfully performed Run 887.

WorkerKit/TEE proves the second claim.

