# 11. Do not send the DEK directly to an alleged TEE

Upgrade our earlier key-release design slightly.

Inside the TEE create a temporary X25519 keypair:

```text
tee_private
tee_public
```

Include:

```text
tee_public
```

inside the attested `report_data`.

After verifying the TDX quote, the key broker encrypts the DEK to that key using **HPKE**.

RFC 9180 defines HPKE and includes the X25519 + HKDF-SHA256 suites suitable for exactly this kind of recipient-specific encrypted key delivery. ([RFC Editor][10])

Flow:

```text
TEE
 │ generates ephemeral X25519 key
 │
 ▼
quote(
  lease_digest,
  asset_digest,
  invocation_id,
  tee_public_key,
  server_nonce
)
 │
 ▼
KEY BROKER
 │
 ├ verify TDX
 ├ verify compose hash
 ├ verify worker image
 ├ verify lease
 ├ verify nonce
 └ verify asset
 │
 ▼
HPKE_encrypt(DEK, tee_public_key)
 │
 ▼
TEE
 │
 └ decrypt worker.af.enc
```

The host/operator never receives the raw package or DEK.

