# 13. ERC-7710 should control wallet capabilities

This standard is almost comically aligned with Moltwork leasing.

ERC-7710 explicitly describes bounded permissions for AI agents and automated systems, long-lived sessions and policy-constrained delegations. It uses ERC-7579 execution semantics and supports ERC-1271/contract accounts. ([Ethereum Improvement Proposals][13])

So separate:

```text
Moltwork Lease
```

from:

```text
Ethereum wallet delegation
```

The lease says:

> what the worker is commercially allowed to do.

ERC-7710 says:

> what Ethereum actions the wallet technically permits it to do.

Example:

```text
Moltwork lease:
    max spend = $10

ERC-7710 caveat:
    USDC transfer <= $10
    only recipient X
    expiry T
```

Both gates must pass.

For modular smart accounts, ERC-7579 defines validators, executors and hooks and requires ERC-1271 compatibility. ([Ethereum Improvement Proposals][14])

This becomes the serious version of:

> rent an autonomous worker without giving it your wallet.

