# 32. Where Moltwork itself remains novel

Almost none of the individual cryptography is ours.

That is good.

Moltwork's protocol is the graph connecting:

```text
exact cognitive state
        +
exact agent configuration
        +
exact execution
        +
exact artifacts
        +
actual cost
        +
independent verification
        +
actual external outcome
        +
actual payment
        +
subsequent learning
```

into:

```text
portable evidence-backed capability
```

Letta doesn't do that.

Phala doesn't do that.

ERC-8004 doesn't do that.

x402 doesn't do that.

ERC-8183 doesn't do that.

Sigstore doesn't do that.

They provide primitives.

Moltwork makes the composite object:

```text
"This exact worker configuration,
with this exact accumulated experience,
has this verified economic history."
```

And `.af + WorkReceipt` are the two objects around which I'd make virtually everything else revolve.

